anger and shock  outside a salt hospital in amman a  one-hour cut of vital oxygen supplies  has been blamed on the deaths of  patients  it affected intensive care maternity and  coronavirus wards  a backup supply arrived too late for  some  ana my father and mother are at the  coronavirus isolation zone inside the  hospital  by coincidence i was inside the hospital  when suddenly the oxygen was cut  we asked off who said they had run out  of oxygen and that they are waiting for  a truck for more supplies  we received assistance from the civil  defense some of them were inside the  hospital  and they provided oxygen cylinders and  then started to resuscitate patients  among them my parents security forces  have been called in  preventing anyone unauthorized from  entering the hospital  these people have no choice but to wait  for news  there was an oxygen outage and there  were no measures to prevent this  it is known that in all jordanian  hospitals there are motors available  just in case electricity goes down  even before the coronavirus outbreak  when there are surgeries at hospitals  there's always spare equipment but here  there was an oxygen outage  i gave my father cpr three times and  twice to my mother  i called the director of the hospital at  10 30. the isolation ward has only one  doctor and two nurses to serve 50 to 60  patients  this is unfair  the fallout was swift health minister  nathir obaid resigned  and king abdullah arrived to a mixed  reception from crowds at the hospital  he immediately ordered the hospital's  director to also resign  parliament has set up a special  committee to investigate  and prime minister bashar al-assad says  there is no justification for what  happened  the government and only the government  takes full responsibility for this very  painful incident  we will not resort to excuses or  justifications about what happened  what happened was horrific so it is  impossible to deny  or to escape responsibility the death of  one jordanian due to these failings  is unacceptable but there are people  here who say the hospital was  understaffed and ill-prepared and many  are asking why a failure like this  went unnoticed until it was too late  laura burden manly al jazeera
 

